Preload the gallium megadriver in the AMD video sandbox hooks.

Our Mesa >= 25 minigbm (openfyde-patches media-libs/minigbm patch 002)
dlopen()s the gallium megadriver by soname "libgallium_dri.so" when it
first allocates a buffer, which in the OOP video decoding utility happens
INSIDE the hardware video decoding sandbox. The existing presandbox
preload of /usr/lib64/dri/radeonsi_dri.so registers the object only under
that path and its versioned SONAME (libgallium-<ver>.so), so ld.so cannot
match the soname request and asks the file broker, which denies library
paths. minigbm's amdgpu backend then fails init, GbmDeviceWrapper has no
device, VaapiVideoDecoder cannot allocate its modifier-probing dummy
buffer, and ALL hardware video decode in the utility dies silently (HEVC
visibly, since it has no software fallback; H.264/VP9 fall back to SW).

Fix: also dlopen the megadriver by that exact soname before entering the
sandbox — glibc dedups by inode and records the name, so the in-sandbox
dlopen resolves from memory. The preload is non-fatal: on Mesa <= 24 the
soname does not exist and minigbm loads radeonsi_dri.so by absolute path
(already preloaded), so AMD systems on older Mesa are unaffected. Same
latent issue fixed in the encode hook (kUseOutOfProcessVideoEncoding is
default-off today).

--- a/media/gpu/sandbox/hardware_video_decoding_sandbox_hook_linux.cc
+++ b/media/gpu/sandbox/hardware_video_decoding_sandbox_hook_linux.cc
@@ -151,6 +151,20 @@
     return false;
   }
 
+  // FydeOS: our Mesa >= 25 minigbm (openfyde-patches minigbm patch 002) loads
+  // the gallium megadriver by soname ("libgallium_dri.so", minigbm dri.c) when
+  // it first allocates inside the sandbox. The preload above registers the
+  // driver only under the radeonsi_dri.so path and its versioned SONAME
+  // (libgallium-<ver>.so), so dlopen it under the soname minigbm asks for as
+  // well; the in-sandbox dlopen() then resolves from the already-loaded object
+  // instead of hitting the (denied) file broker. The soname does not exist on
+  // Mesa <= 24 installs, where minigbm loads radeonsi_dri.so by absolute path
+  // (already preloaded above), so failure to preload it is not fatal.
+  if (nullptr == dlopen("libgallium_dri.so", kDlopenFlags)) {
+    LOG(WARNING) << "dlopen(libgallium_dri.so) failed with error: "
+                 << dlerror();
+  }
+
   // minigbm may use the DRI driver (requires Mesa 24.0 or older) or the
   // Vulkan driver (requires VK_EXT_image_drm_format_modifier).  Preload the
   // Vulkan driver as well but ignore failures.
--- a/media/gpu/sandbox/hardware_video_encoding_sandbox_hook_linux.cc
+++ b/media/gpu/sandbox/hardware_video_encoding_sandbox_hook_linux.cc
@@ -125,6 +125,15 @@
       return false;
     }
 
+    // FydeOS: preload the gallium megadriver under the soname our Mesa >= 25
+    // minigbm dlopen()s inside the sandbox (see the equivalent preload and
+    // rationale in hardware_video_decoding_sandbox_hook_linux.cc). Missing on
+    // Mesa <= 24 installs, so not fatal.
+    if (nullptr == dlopen("libgallium_dri.so", kDlopenFlags)) {
+      LOG(WARNING) << "dlopen(libgallium_dri.so) failed with error: "
+                   << dlerror();
+    }
+
     // minigbm may use the DRI driver (requires Mesa 24.0 or older) or the
     // Vulkan driver (requires VK_EXT_image_drm_format_modifier).  Preload the
     // Vulkan driver as well but ignore failures.
